# star24full k=8 — 2026-08-07

Landed solver (fixes 1-9 + static face filter + pair filter + dynamic face-closure filter). Uncapped.
Pooled: 400 shards through 9 slots — doubled from k=7's 200 because the k=7 parallel floor was the
slowest single shard, 218 s of 1109 total CPU-s (20%). Finer shards only help if that shard held more
than one heavy first-type subtree; if one type dominates it, the floor does not move.

Projection from the ladder (k5 46.2 s, k6 198 s, k7 1109 CPU-s; time ratio falling 8.7 -> 5.5 -> 4.3):
expect roughly 3,500-4,500 CPU-s, so 8-12 min wall on 9 slots. Count projection ~2.0x k=7 => ~6,400,
cumulative ~12,600.

